     <div style="background: #fff;
                    width: 90%;
                    margin-right: auto;
                    margin-left: auto;">
                   Dear {!Contact.FirstName}, <br /><br />

<b>Student ID: {!Contact.EMPLID__c}</b><br /><br />

Thank you for submitting your application for graduation from Arizona State University. At this time, <b>your application has been denied</b> for the following reason(s): <br /><br />

<ul>
<li>You have not completed the total hours required for your degree <b>and</b> you have not indicated an adequate number of potential transfer credits. The university requires a minimum of 120 total credit hours. 
</li> <br /><br />

<li>You have not completed the total upper division hours required for your degree 
<b>and</b> you have not indicated an adequate number of potential upper division transfer credits. The university requires a minimum of 45 (51 for business degrees) total upper division credit hours. </li> <br /><br />
</ul>	

<b><i>Please speak with your advisor if you have questions.</i></b> If corrections need to be made to your record, or if you are transferring in hours from another institution, please contact the Graduation office at <a href="mailto:graduation@asu.edu"> graduation@asu.edu</a> or 480-965-3256. <b>It is imperative that you contact the Graduation office to avoid your immediate withdrawal from the graduation process.</b>  If you will not meet the requirements in the original semester you requested, you will need to reapply, with no additional fee, for a future graduation date.<br /><br />

Sincerely,<br />

{!Case.OwnerFullName}<br /><br />

        <div style="color:#990033;font-family: Arial, Helvetica !important;">
